---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { PUBLIC_SITE_URL } from 'astro:env/client';

const seoTitle = 'Comegame Withdrawal Guide: How to Cash Out Winnings Safely in India';
const seoDescription =
	'Step-by-step guide to withdrawing winnings on Comegame — UPI withdrawals, KYC requirements, minimum amounts, timelines, common problems, and tax tips for Indian users.';
const canonicalUrl = `${PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/blog/comegame-withdrawal-guide`;
const ogImage = `${PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/android-chrome-512x512.png`;
const keywordsMeta =
	'comegame withdrawal, come game cashout, comegame UPI withdrawal, comegame withdrawal time india, comegame KYC withdrawal, online gaming withdrawal india, comegame payout guide';

const articleSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'BlogPosting',
	headline: seoTitle,
	description: seoDescription,
	url: canonicalUrl,
	image: ogImage,
	datePublished: '2026-07-01',
	dateModified: '2026-07-01',
	inLanguage: 'en-IN',
	author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Come Game Guide' },
	publisher: {
		'@type': 'Organization',
		name: 'Come Game Guide',
		logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: ogImage },
	},
	mainEntityOfPage: canonicalUrl,
};

const faqSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'FAQPage',
	mainEntity: [
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'How long does a Comegame withdrawal take?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Most Comegame withdrawals via UPI are processed within a few hours to 24 hours once KYC is complete and the request passes internal verification. Bank transfer withdrawals may take 1–3 working days.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'What is the minimum withdrawal amount on Comegame?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'The minimum withdrawal amount on Comegame is typically ₹100, though this may vary. Check the platform\'s current withdrawal policy in your account settings for the most accurate figure.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Why is my Comegame withdrawal pending?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Common reasons include incomplete KYC verification, unmet bonus wagering requirements, name mismatch between the account and the linked payment method, or the request being queued during high-volume periods.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Is TDS deducted on Comegame withdrawals?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Yes. Under Indian tax law, TDS at 30% is applicable on net winnings from online gaming that exceed specified thresholds. The platform deducts TDS before crediting the net amount to your payment method.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Can I withdraw Comegame bonus money directly?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'No. Bonus credits are not directly withdrawable. You must meet the applicable wagering requirements first, after which the resulting winnings become withdrawable as real money.',
			},
		},
	],
};
---

<Layout
	title={seoTitle}
	description={seoDescription}
	keywords={keywordsMeta}
	canonical={canonicalUrl}
	ogImage={ogImage}
>
	<Fragment slot="head">
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)}></script>
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)}></script>
	</Fragment>

	<article class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12 md:py-16">
		<header class="max-w-4xl">
			<a href="/blog" class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-border bg-card px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
				Back to Blog
			</a>
			<h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-5xl">
				Comegame Withdrawal Guide: How to Cash Out Winnings Safely in India
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-muted-foreground">Published on July 1, 2026 | Withdrawals &amp; Payments Guide</p>
			<p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground md:text-lg">
				Withdrawing winnings should be one of the simplest actions on any gaming platform. In practice, Indian
				users encounter a range of friction points — pending requests, failed transactions, KYC holds, and
				confusion about tax deductions — that turn the cashout process into a source of stress. This guide
				walks through every step of the Comegame withdrawal process, explains why problems occur, and gives
				practical fixes for the most common issues.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="mt-8 max-w-5xl overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card/50 p-5">
			<div class="grid items-center gap-4 md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr]">
				<img src="/logo.svg" alt="Comegame withdrawal guide India" class="h-16 w-16 rounded-xl border border-border bg-background p-2" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
				<p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
					Before requesting a withdrawal, ensure your KYC is fully verified and your linked payment method
					matches the name on your account. Read our
					<a href="/blog/comegame-account-setup-guide" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">account setup and KYC guide</a>
					if you have not completed verification yet. Incomplete verification is the leading cause of delayed withdrawals.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<section class="mt-10 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Understanding the Comegame Wallet Structure</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Before you request a withdrawal, you need to understand how your Comegame wallet is structured. Most
				Indian gaming platforms, including Comegame, divide your balance into at least two distinct buckets:
				your real-money balance (also called cash balance or withdrawable balance) and your bonus balance.
				These are not interchangeable.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Your real-money balance consists of funds you deposited directly plus any winnings that have been
				cleared for withdrawal (that is, winnings derived from real-money play or from bonus play after the
				wagering requirement has been met). Only this balance is withdrawable. Your bonus balance holds credits
				from welcome offers, referral rewards, or promotions — these cannot be withdrawn directly and must be
				wagered according to the applicable terms before converting to withdrawable funds.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Some platforms further subdivide the real-money balance into "deposit balance" and "winnings balance,"
				with the deposit portion subject to a minimum withdrawal requirement or a brief hold period after a
				fresh deposit. Understanding these distinctions prevents confusion when you see your total balance is
				₹1,500 but the withdrawal screen only shows ₹800 as available. For a broader overview of how Comegame's
				finances work, see our
				<a href="/real-money-come-games" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">real money Come Games guide</a>
				which covers deposits, wallet management, and the flow of funds from deposit to winnings.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">KYC Requirements Before You Can Withdraw</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				KYC — Know Your Customer — is the identity verification process required by Indian law for platforms
				handling real money. On Comegame, you must complete KYC before your first withdrawal is processed,
				and in many cases, before you can withdraw any amount above a basic threshold. Skipping KYC during
				registration and only attempting it when you want to withdraw is one of the most common mistakes users
				make, because it causes delays precisely when you want the process to be fast.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The standard KYC documents required on Indian gaming platforms are: a government-issued photo ID
				(Aadhaar card, PAN card, passport, or voter ID) and proof of address. PAN card specifically is often
				mandatory on gaming platforms because it is required for TDS compliance. Some platforms also require
				a bank account statement or cancelled cheque for payment method verification.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				After submission, KYC verification typically takes between a few hours and two business days. During
				this period, your withdrawal requests may be queued rather than immediately processed. Our
				<a href="/blog/comegame-account-setup-guide" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame account setup guide</a>
				covers the full KYC process in detail — what documents to prepare, how to photograph them correctly,
				and what to do if verification is rejected.
			</p>
			<h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Why Name Matching Matters</h3>
			<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				One of the most common KYC rejection reasons is a name mismatch. The name on your Comegame account
				must exactly match the name on your KYC document AND the name on your linked UPI or bank account.
				If you registered with a nickname, an abbreviated name, or made a typo, the verification will fail
				or your withdrawal will be held for manual review. Correct this in your profile settings before
				submitting KYC documents.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Step-by-Step: How to Withdraw on Comegame</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Once your KYC is approved and you have a withdrawable balance, the process itself is straightforward.
				Here is a complete walkthrough.
			</p>
			<ol class="mt-5 list-decimal space-y-5 pl-6 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Open the app and navigate to your Wallet or Account section.</strong>
					Look for a "Withdraw" or "Cash Out" button. It is usually prominently placed on the wallet screen.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Verify your available withdrawable balance.</strong>
					Confirm the amount shown matches your expectation. If the available amount is lower than your
					total balance, the difference is likely held in bonus credits or is subject to a pending
					wagering requirement.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Select your withdrawal method.</strong>
					For most Indian users, UPI is the fastest and most convenient option. Other methods may include
					IMPS bank transfer or net banking. UPI typically processes faster than a direct bank transfer.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Enter or confirm your UPI ID or bank account details.</strong>
					If you have already linked a payment method in your profile settings, it may auto-populate. Verify
					the details are correct before proceeding. A withdrawal sent to the wrong account cannot be reversed
					easily.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Enter the withdrawal amount.</strong>
					Ensure the amount is above the platform's minimum withdrawal threshold (typically ₹100). There
					may also be a daily or weekly maximum withdrawal limit — check the platform's current policy if
					you are withdrawing a large amount.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Confirm with OTP or PIN.</strong>
					Most platforms require a one-time password sent to your registered mobile number to authorise
					the withdrawal. Enter it accurately. Do not share this OTP with anyone — no legitimate platform
					support agent will ask for it.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Note the reference number and wait for processing.</strong>
					After confirmation, a reference number is generated. Save this. If your withdrawal does not
					arrive within the stated timeline, use this reference number when contacting support.
				</li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">UPI Withdrawals: Speed, Limits, and Best Practices</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				UPI (Unified Payments Interface) is the dominant payment method for Indian gaming platform withdrawals
				for good reason. Transactions are near-instant when the system is running smoothly, the infrastructure
				is widely available, and most users already have a UPI-linked bank account set up via apps like GPay,
				PhonePe, or Paytm. Comegame supports UPI withdrawals, making it the recommended method for most users.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				A few practical notes about UPI withdrawals: the UPI ID you use for withdrawal must be linked to a
				bank account registered in your name. Third-party UPI IDs — a friend's, a family member's — will
				typically be rejected during verification because the account holder name will not match your KYC
				details. Ensure you enter the full UPI VPA (Virtual Payment Address) correctly; even one wrong
				character will cause the transaction to fail.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				UPI has a per-transaction limit of ₹1 lakh set by NPCI (National Payments Corporation of India),
				though individual banks may apply lower limits. If you are withdrawing a large amount, check whether
				your bank's UPI limit accommodates it. For amounts above your UPI limit, a bank transfer via NEFT
				or IMPS may be more appropriate. The platform will display available methods based on your withdrawal
				amount.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Withdrawal Timelines: What to Expect</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Withdrawal processing has two phases: the platform's internal processing time, and the payment network's
				transfer time. The internal processing is where most variation occurs.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				For fully verified accounts with straightforward requests, Comegame typically processes withdrawal
				requests within a few hours to 24 hours. During this phase, the platform's system verifies that
				the request meets all conditions: withdrawable balance is sufficient, no active bonus wagering
				requirement blocks the funds, KYC is complete, and the payment details match. If all conditions
				are met automatically, the request moves to the payment stage quickly.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				If the platform's system flags a request for manual review — typically for large amounts, first-time
				withdrawals, or security triggers — the timeline extends. Manual review can add one to three business
				days. After the platform releases the funds, UPI transfers typically arrive within minutes. NEFT
				transfers arrive within 2 hours during banking hours (cut-off batches apply); IMPS is near-instant.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				If your withdrawal has not arrived within 3 business days and you have a reference number, contact
				Comegame's support team via the
				<a href="/contact" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">contact page</a>.
				Provide the reference number, withdrawal amount, and date of request. This gives the support team
				everything they need to investigate without a back-and-forth delay.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Common Withdrawal Problems and Their Fixes</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Understanding why withdrawals fail is more useful than simply knowing what to do when they do. Here
				are the most frequently encountered problems and the specific actions that resolve them.
			</p>
			<div class="mt-5 space-y-6">
				<div>
					<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Problem: Withdrawal button greyed out or unavailable</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
						This usually indicates that your KYC is incomplete, your account has an active wagering
						requirement that covers your current balance, or you have not yet made a deposit of the
						minimum required amount. Check each of these conditions in your account settings. If KYC
						is pending, complete and submit it. For wagering requirements, check the bonus section to
						see how much playthrough remains.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Problem: Withdrawal rejected with "name mismatch" error</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
						Your account name, KYC document name, and linked UPI or bank account name must all match
						exactly. Update your profile to correct any discrepancy. If the mismatch is in your KYC
						document itself (for example, an Aadhaar with an old name), update the document first or
						use an alternative document that matches your current legal name.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Problem: Withdrawal stuck in "Processing" for more than 48 hours</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
						This often indicates a manual review queue. Contact support with your reference number.
						If this is your first withdrawal, it is normal for the platform to apply additional
						verification steps. Subsequent withdrawals from the same account typically process faster.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Problem: Amount received is less than expected</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
						The difference is almost always TDS. If your net winnings exceed the applicable threshold,
						the platform deducts TDS at 30% before transferring the remainder. Your account dashboard
						should show a breakdown of the gross amount, TDS deducted, and net amount transferred.
						Retain this for your income tax return. For more on TDS, see the tax section later in this guide.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Problem: UPI transfer failed but amount was deducted from Comegame wallet</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
						In rare cases, the payment gateway processes the deduction from the platform wallet but the
						UPI transfer fails at the bank end. In such scenarios, the amount is typically auto-reversed
						to your Comegame wallet within 24–72 hours. If it does not appear, raise a dispute with
						your UPI provider (Google Pay, PhonePe, etc.) and also contact Comegame support simultaneously.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Bonus Wagering and Its Effect on Withdrawals</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				If you have claimed any bonus on Comegame, an active wagering requirement may restrict which portion
				of your balance you can withdraw. This is one of the most misunderstood aspects of gaming platform
				finances. Many users see a healthy balance and attempt a withdrawal, only to find the system blocks
				it because a bonus wagering condition is still active.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The rule is: funds subject to an active wagering requirement are not withdrawable until that requirement
				is either met or the bonus is forfeited. If you want to withdraw immediately without meeting the
				wagering condition, most platforms allow you to forfeit the bonus — but this means the bonus credits
				disappear and any winnings derived specifically from bonus play may also be removed.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Before accepting any bonus, read the terms carefully. Our
				<a href="/blog/comegame-bonus-guide-india" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame bonus guide for India</a>
				explains wagering requirements in full detail, including how to calculate whether a bonus is
				realistic to clear given your typical play volume. Understanding this before claiming prevents
				the situation where a bonus blocks your legitimate winnings from being withdrawn.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Tax Implications: TDS on Gaming Winnings in India</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				India's tax framework for online gaming has become significantly clearer in recent years. Under the
				current provisions of the Income Tax Act (as amended), online gaming platforms are required to deduct
				TDS (Tax Deducted at Source) at 30% on net winnings at the time of withdrawal. The threshold and
				calculation method have evolved — as of recent amendments, TDS applies to net winnings without any
				basic exemption threshold for online games specifically designated under the tax framework.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Net winnings are calculated as: total amount withdrawn minus total amount deposited (in simplified
				terms). The platform tracks this on a financial-year basis. When you withdraw, the platform's system
				calculates the applicable TDS, deducts it, and transfers the net amount to your account. You will
				receive a Form 26AS or TDS certificate reflecting the deducted amount, which you use when filing
				your annual income tax return.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				There are a few important nuances. First, TDS is not the same as your final tax liability — it is
				a prepayment. If you fall in a lower income tax bracket or have losses from other sources, you may
				be entitled to a refund on the TDS amount when you file your return. Second, gaming winnings are
				taxed at a flat 30% rate regardless of your income slab — unlike salary income where different slabs
				apply. Third, you cannot set off gaming losses against gaming winnings for tax purposes under current
				Indian tax law.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				For specific and personalised tax advice, consult a qualified chartered accountant who is familiar
				with online gaming taxation. The
				<a href="/faq" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame FAQ section</a>
				also addresses common tax questions in a general informational format. Do not rely solely on platform
				estimates for your tax obligations — verify with an official source or tax professional.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Responsible Money Management for Gaming Withdrawals</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The act of withdrawing winnings is not just a technical process — it is also a financial decision.
				How you handle winnings determines whether gaming remains a sustainable entertainment activity or
				becomes a source of financial instability. Here are the principles that experienced, responsible
				players follow.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				First, set a "withdraw threshold" before you start playing. Decide in advance: if my balance reaches
				₹X, I will withdraw ₹Y. This prevents the common pattern of continually reinvesting winnings until
				you have lost everything. Treat a portion of winnings as actual earnings — withdraw and bank them,
				rather than keeping all funds in the gaming wallet.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Second, never play with withdrawn funds in the same session. If you have decided to withdraw and
				lock in a win, do not second-guess the decision when the next game starts. The urge to "let it ride"
				is a well-documented cognitive bias — resisting it is a skill that separates disciplined players from
				those who watch winnings evaporate.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Third, keep a simple monthly log of deposits and withdrawals. At the end of each month, calculate
				your net position. This is both useful for tax purposes (as it tracks your net winnings for TDS
				calculations) and for honest self-assessment of whether gaming is profitable or costing you money.
				Most players overestimate their wins and underestimate their losses when relying purely on memory.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The broader framework for responsible play — including deposit limits, time limits, and self-exclusion
				options — is covered in our
				<a href="/responsible-gaming" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">responsible gaming guide</a>.
				This should be a mandatory read before you make any real-money deposit on Comegame or any other platform.
				Gaming is entertainment, and withdrawals are a sign that you have played responsibly when they reflect
				genuine net gains rather than recouped losses.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Security During the Withdrawal Process</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Withdrawal requests are a sensitive moment from a security standpoint because they involve real money
				in transit. This makes gaming accounts a target for social engineering attacks. Here is what to watch
				for and how to protect yourself.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Fraudulent "support agents" frequently contact users — via WhatsApp, social media, or email — claiming
				to be from Comegame support and offering to "expedite" pending withdrawals. They ask for your OTP,
				PIN, password, or account access. Legitimate platform support will never ask for these. No support
				interaction requires you to share your OTP. If anyone asks for it, it is a scam — disconnect and
				report it. Use only the official support channel linked from the
				<a href="/contact" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">contact page</a>.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Also ensure your Comegame account password is not reused from another service. If a different platform
				you use suffers a data breach and your credentials are exposed, attackers may attempt to use those
				same credentials on your Comegame account. Enable two-factor authentication if the platform offers
